  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Loma Linda University 2026-2027 Catalog (effective Summer Quarter 2026) program page 'Diagnostic Medical Sonography - B.S.', Cardiac concentration (School of Allied Health Professions, Department of Radiation Technology). 24-month curriculum (8 quarters) leading to eligibility for the ARDMS RDCS board examinations. The catalog publishes the curriculum split by 8 quarters; quarter sums verified: 12, 13, 12, 11, 14, 14, 12, 12 = 100 = the curriculum table's Total Units 100. Note: the page's prerequisite text states cardiac students 'will earn 101 units in the program,' which is inconsistent with the official curriculum table (Total Units: 100); the table is transcribed because it is internally consistent and authoritative for the sequence. The cardiac concentration's clinical quarters are published under 'General Vascular Clinical Affiliation' course numbers (RTMS 371, 372, 373, 471); transcribed verbatim. Per-course prerequisites stated in the catalog: RTMS 372 requires RTMS 371; RTMS 373 requires RTMS 372. The remaining published quarter order is the official sequence, so other prereq arrays are intentionally empty. All students must pass the ARDMS Sonography Principles and Instrumentation (SPI) exam while enrolled. Prerequisites (91 quarter / 61 semester units including the published GE domains; 3.0 GPA; information session; interview) are documented here and not placed in any term.",
